        "title": "02 - Propulsion",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "IDEAL OTTO CYCLE (p-v diagram):\n  1→2: isentropic compression (piston up; adiabatic)\n  2→3: constant-volume heat addition (spark ignition; combustion)\n  3→4: isentropic expansion (power stroke)\n  4→1: constant-volume heat rejection (exhaust valve opens)"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-PROPULSION.md#011",
      "path": [
        "02-PROPULSION.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:aeronautics:02-propulsion, git-history:aeronautics:02-propulsion]",
        "canonical_path": "aeronautics/02-PROPULSION.md",
        "concepts": "[propulsion]",
        "current_path": "aeronautics/02-PROPULSION.md",
        "id": "maxim:aeronautics:propulsion",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "aeronautics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[propulsion]",
        "section": "aeronautics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "02 - Propulsion",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THERMAL EFFICIENCY:\n  η_th = 1 − 1/r^(γ-1)\n  r = compression ratio = V_BDC / V_TDC\n  γ = 1.4 for air (diatomic)\n  Higher compression → higher efficiency → knock (pre-ignition) limits r to ~8-12 for gasoline\n  Diesel cycle: constant-pressure combustion; higher r (14-22); higher efficiency; no knock"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-PROPULSION.md#012",
      "path": [
        "02-PROPULSION.md"
