        "section": "aeronautics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "02 - Propulsion",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "AIRCRAFT PISTON ENGINES:\n  Horizontally opposed (flat): Lycoming, Continental; 4-6 cylinders; 100-300 hp\n  Air-cooled: weight advantage; no coolant system\n  Fuel: avgas 100LL (100 octane, low lead); moving toward unleaded UL94/UL100\n  Turbocharged/supercharged: maintain manifold pressure at altitude (normally aspirated engines\n    lose power with altitude: power ∝ ρ ∝ p)\n  Magneto ignition: redundant dual magneto system (not battery-dependent)\n  Constant-speed propeller: governor adjusts pitch to maintain rpm → optimal efficiency\n```"
    },
