      "text": "Thermodynamic context: eta_Brayton = 1 - 1/OPR^((gamma-1)/gamma) = 1 - T1/T2, which approaches but never reaches the Carnot limit eta_Carnot = 1 - T1/T3 (where T3 = turbine inlet temperature). High OPR raises T2 (compressor exit), improving efficiency. Real gas turbines achieve ~40-45% thermal efficiency, roughly 60% of the Carnot limit for the same temperature extremes. Combined cycle plants (gas turbine + steam Rankine on exhaust heat) reach ~60% thermal efficiency — closest any thermal engine gets to Carnot at scale."
